'''Shinmei Shrine''' (神明神社) is a [[Shinto shrine]] located in [[Sōja, Okayama|Sōja City]], [[Okayama Prefecture]], Japan.

## Overview
The shrine was historically the tutelary deity of [[Abe Village (Okayama)|Abe Village]] (阿部村) in [[Kayo District, Bitchū Province|Kayo District, Bitchū Province]].<ref>Abe Village was located in what is now southern Fukui, Sōja City. In [[1881]] (Meiji 14), it merged with Fukui Village.</ref> The enshrined deity is [[Amaterasu Ōmikami]], and the shrine is associated with the [[Ise Grand Shrine]], specifically the [[Kōtai Jingū]] (Inner Shrine). 

The shrine’s sacred messenger is the [[chicken]] (long-crowing bird), which played a role in luring Amaterasu out of the [[Ama-no-Iwato]] (Heavenly Rock Cave).

An excerpt from the lost [[Fudoki]] of Bitchū Province, titled *Miyasegawa* (宮瀬川), states that in Kayo District, there was a river to the east of the *Ise Mikami no Yashiro* (伊勢御神社), and to the west of the river stood the *Kibi Takehiko no Mikoto no Miya* (吉備建日子命宮). This river was thus called *Miyasegawa*. Some theories equate *Ise Mikami no Yashiro* with Shinmei Shrine, though this remains uncertain. Additionally, records indicate that the shrine was known as *Motoise Nakatahama Shrine* in several historical texts.

Today, the shrine operates independently.

## Sub-Shrines
* Kōjin Shrine (荒神社)
* Ji Shrine (地神社)
* Kin Shrine (金神神社)
* Kimoto Shrine & Shōden Shrine (木本宮・正殿宮)
* Nanasha Shrine (七社宮)

